Wrong fix: uses the attachment's model_type as the role name. That
works for "part", where model and role share a name, but no role is
named "stockitem" (stock items sit under the "stock" role). So no
non-superuser can see a stock item's attachments any more, even with
stock view permission. Secure, but the both-roles regression test must
catch it.

